====Verb====
{{en-verb}}

# {{lb|en|intransitive}} To make sudden loud noises, often repeatedly, especially by exploding or hitting something.
#: {{ux|en|The fireworks '''banged''' away all through the night.}}
#: {{ux|en|The door '''banged''' in the wind.}}
#: {{ux|en|My head was '''banging''' after drinking all night at the concert.}}
# {{lb|en|transitive}} To hit (something) hard, making a loud noise.
#: {{ux|en|She '''banged''' the table with her fist.}}
#: {{ux|en|He '''banged''' the drum in sync with the band.}}
#: {{ux|en|Hold the picture while I '''bang''' in this nail.}}
#* {{RQ:Shakespeare Othello|act=II|scene=i|passage=The desperate tempest hath so '''banged''' the Turks.}}
# {{lb|en|transitive}} To cause or suffer (one thing) to hit (another).
#: {{ux|en|The blacksmith '''banged''' the hammer on the anvil.}}
#: {{ux|en|I '''banged''' my head on the ceiling.}}
#: {{ux|en|He '''banged''' the door shut.}}
#* {{quote-book|en|year=1922|author=w:Michael Arlen|title=[http://openlibrary.org/works/OL1519647W “Piracy”: A Romantic Chronicle of These Days]|chapter=3/19/2| passage=Ivor had acquired more than a mile of fishing rights with the house; he was not at all a good fisherman, but one must do something; one generally, however, '''banged''' a ball with a squash-racket against a wall.}}
# {{lb|en|intransitive|generally with a preposition}} To hit (on, against, etc. something).
#: {{ux|en|Stop '''banging''' on the door. I heard you the first time!}}
#: {{ux|en|My knee '''banged''' against the rung of the ladder.}}
#: {{ux|en|David and Mary '''banged''' into each other.}}
# {{lb|en|slang|ambitransitive|vulgar}} To engage in [[sexual intercourse]].
#: {{syn|en|nail|do it|have sex|Thesaurus:copulate|Thesaurus:copulate with}}
#: {{ux|en|We can hear the couple '''banging''' upstairs.}}
#* {{quote-av|en|writer=w:Cameron Crowe|title=w:Jerry Maguire|year=1996|actor=w:Jay Mohr|role=Bob Sugar|location=Culver City, Calif.|publisher=w:TriStar Pictures; distributed by [[w:Sony Pictures Home Entertainment|Columbia TriStar Home Video]]|year_published=1997|isbn=978-0-8001-4174-5|passage=<!--ORIGINAL TEXT: "<span style="font-variant:small-caps">Jerry Maguire</span>: ". However, the citation of this same quotation at "[[skank]]" states that the line was said by Bob Sugar. Please verify.-->It's also my job to take care of the [[skank]]s on the road that you '''bang'''.}}
#* {{quote-av|en|year=1972|writers=w:Mario Puzo; w:Francis Ford Coppola|title=w:The Godfather|passage=<span style="font-variant:small-caps">Moe Greene:</span> He was '''banging''' cocktail waitresses two at a time!}}
# {{lb|en|transitive}} To cut squarely across, as the tail of a horse, or a person's forelock; to cut (the hair).
#* {{quote-book|en|year=c. 1883|author=w:Frank Hamilton Cushing|title=Becomin a Zuni
|passage=His hair '''banged''' even with his eyebrows.}}
# {{lb|en|transitive|slang|drugs}} To [[inject]] intravenously.
#: {{ux|en|Do you smoke meth? No, I '''bang''' it.}}
# {{lb|en|finance|transitive|dated}} To depress the prices in (a market).
#* {{quote-book|en|year=1821|author=Bank of England|title=The Bank - The Stock Exchange - The Bankers ...|page=64
|passage=This accompt has been made to appear a bull accompt, ''i.e.'' that the bulls cannot take their stock. The fact is the reverse; it is a bear accompt, but the bears, unable to deliver their stock, have conjointly '''banged''' the market, and pocketed the tickets, to defeat the rise and loss that would have ensued to them by their buying on a rising price on the accompt day {{...}}}}
#* {{quote-journal|en|year=1902|journal=Truth|volume=50|page=1138
|passage={{...}} the London "Bears" have promptly banged the market again {{...}}}}
# {{lb|en|slang|transitive|obsolete}} To [[excel]] or [[surpass]]. <!--Hotten's slang dict. 1873-->
# {{lb|en|intransitive|stative|slang}} To be [[excellent]]; to be [[banging]]
#: {{syn|en|eat|rule|rock|slap|Thesaurus:excel}}
#: {{ux|en|This song '''bangs'''!}}
# {{lb|en|Nigeria|slang}} To [[fail]], especially an [[exam]]; to [[flunk]].
# {{lb|en|New England|slang|intransitive}} To make a [[turn]] in a vehicle; to [[hang a right]], [[hang a left|left]], or [[hang a uey|uey]].
#: {{ux|en|'''Bang''' a right at the next stoplight.}}
# {{lb|en|US|_|slang|}} To [[gangbang]]; to participate in street gang criminal activity.
#: {{ux|en|You know I still '''bang'''.}}
# {{lb|en|sports}} To play a [[sport]] aggressively.

